finding: Coverage is lost in view-model's shared evidence page. In examples/view-model/tests/stepped.html, contact/depth/count restore part RenderLayers with mask(2), not the parts' original masks. A response-only plant in src/scene.ts initialized the first part with mask 0 instead of 2. Fresh-page count returned 2 (fails its exactly-three assertion); the shared sequence returned contact=13365, depth={overlap:0,exposed:2968}, count=3, fov=0, light=4944, so every evidence claim passed. Contact repaired the planted defect before count observed it. Smallest fix: save/restore each part's actual mask in evidence calls instead of restoring the expected constant, with a regression proving count still rejects an initially hidden part after contact/depth. The cheap scene test also checks masks, but that does not preserve this browser claim's former coverage. Separately, holdFrames changes cancelAnimationFrame semantics during dispatch: __shallotRunHeldFrames snapshots values and clears held before invoking callbacks, so callback A cannot cancel held callback B due in the same frame. Independent Chromium reproduction yielded ['a','b'] after A called cancelAnimationFrame(b), rather than ['a']; a callback queued by A ran once on the next run. Smallest fix: snapshot ids, consult/delete each live entry immediately before invoking it, so canceled entries are skipped and new entries wait for the next frame; add the same-frame cancellation case. Baseline browser checks pass despite both defects.
